# Competition Web App API v1: every endpoint plus error examples.
# Open in VS Code with the free "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client)
# and click "Send Request" above any request. Start the server first: npm run dev
# (also works in JetBrains IDEs' built-in HTTP client). Reference: docs/API.md

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5050

# ==================== Service ====================

### Health
# Service status, versions and data timestamp. Expect 200. Never cached.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/health

### Parameters
# Label, unit, decimals, aggregation and intervals of every series key. Expect 200.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/parameters

### Parameter
# One parameter by key. Expect 200.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/parameters/rain

# ==================== Areas ====================

### List areas
# Every area with region, center and data coverage. Expect 200.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/areas

### List cities with boundary and layers
# type filter plus embedded extras (include=* gives all). Expect 200.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/areas?type=city&include=boundary,layers

### Area
# One area. Expect 200.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/areas/jaipur

### Area with layers
# One area with its map layers embedded. Expect 200.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/areas/jaisalmer?include=layers

### Boundary
# District outline as a GeoJSON Feature. Expect 200.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/areas/jaipur/boundary

# ==================== Timeseries ====================

### Timeseries (several areas)
# NDVI and rainfall for two cities, Jan 2015 to Dec 2020 inclusive. Missing months are null. Expect 200.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/timeseries?areas=jaipur,delhi&parameters=ndvi,rain&from=2015-01&to=2020-12&interval=monthly

### Timeseries (everything)
# Every area and every parameter for the full range. Expect 200.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/timeseries?areas=*&parameters=*

### Timeseries (every city)
# type filters areas=* like on /areas (what the website loads at startup). Expect 200.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/timeseries?areas=*&type=city&parameters=*&interval=monthly

### Timeseries (type with no areas)
# No area has type custom yet, so data.areas is {}. Expect 200.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/timeseries?areas=*&type=custom&parameters=ndvi&from=2026-01

### Area timeseries
# One area; parameters default to all. A range reaching outside the data is clipped. Expect 200.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/areas/jaipur/timeseries?parameters=ndvi,rain&from=2024-01&to=2030-12

# ==================== Layers ====================

### Layers
# Map layers of an area: bounds, times, image paths, values link. Expect 200.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/areas/jaipur/layers

### Layers (Jaisalmer, incl. Sentinel-2)
# Jaisalmer also has three Sentinel-2 10 m image layers. Expect 200.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/areas/jaisalmer/layers

### Layer
# One layer. Expect 200.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/areas/jaipur/layers/ndvi-peak

### Layer values (one time)
# Stored integer grid for 2020; multiply by scale (0.001) for NDVI. Expect 200.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/areas/jaipur/layers/ndvi-peak/values?time=2020

### Layer values (all times)
# A timed layer without time returns every year: { "2010": grid, ... }. Expect 200.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/areas/jaipur/layers/ndvi-peak/values

### Layer values (one time, checked format)
# time is written in the layer's interval (ndvi-peak: yearly, YYYY). Expect 200.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/areas/udaipur/layers/ndvi-peak/values?time=2026

### Layer values (static)
# Summer daytime land surface temperature grid; multiply by 0.1 for °C. Expect 200.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/areas/jaipur/layers/lst-day-summer/values

# ==================== Basemap ====================

### Basemap
# Bounds, zoom, image and label paths of every mosaic. Expect 200.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/basemap

# ==================== Errors ====================

### Unknown area
# Expect 404 not_found.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/areas/atlantis

### Unknown parameter in query
# Expect 400 invalid_parameter (details.unknown, details.valid).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/timeseries?areas=jaipur&parameters=ndvi,bogus

### Missing areas
# areas is required on /timeseries. Expect 400 invalid_query.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/timeseries?parameters=ndvi

### Bad month
# from must be YYYY-MM for monthly data. Expect 400 invalid_query.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/areas/jaipur/timeseries?from=2020-13

### from after to
# Expect 400 invalid_query.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/areas/jaipur/timeseries?from=2021-01&to=2020-12

### Unknown include
# Expect 400 invalid_query (details.allowed).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/areas?include=forecast

### Unsupported interval
# Only monthly exists today. Expect 400 unsupported_interval (details.supported).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/timeseries?areas=jaipur&interval=daily

### Layer-only interval
# yearly describes layer times, it is not a timeseries interval. Expect 400 unsupported_interval (details.supported = ["monthly"]).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/timeseries?areas=jaipur&parameters=ndvi&interval=yearly

### Parameter without the interval
# A parameter named in the list must offer the interval; otherwise 400
# unsupported_interval with details { interval, parameter, supported } (with
# parameters=* such parameters are left out instead). Every parameter is
# monthly today, so this query only shows the shape. Expect 200.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/timeseries?areas=jaipur&parameters=ndvi,rain&interval=monthly&from=2026-01

### Response too large
# areas x parameters x times above the limit (TIMESERIES_MAX_VALUES, default
# 500000) is 400 invalid_query with details.limit and details.requested. The
# full data is 6 x 16 x 201 = 19296 values, so this needs a server started with
# a small limit, e.g. TIMESERIES_MAX_VALUES=1000 npm start. Expect 400 invalid_query there, 200 with the default.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/timeseries?areas=*&parameters=*

### Unknown layer time
# Well formed (YYYY) but not in the layer's times. Expect 404 not_found (details.times).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/areas/jaipur/layers/ndvi-peak/values?time=1999

### Malformed layer time
# ndvi-peak is yearly, so a month is the wrong format. Expect 400 invalid_query (details.format = "YYYY").
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/areas/jaipur/layers/ndvi-peak/values?time=2020-06

### time on a static layer
# Static layers have one grid. Expect 400 invalid_query.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/areas/jaipur/layers/ndvi-change/values?time=2020

### Layer without values
# Sentinel-2 layers are images only. Expect 404 not_found.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/areas/jaisalmer/layers/s2-ndvi/values

### Wrong method
# Only GET (and HEAD) are supported. Expect 405 method_not_allowed with an Allow header.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/areas
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Unknown route
# Expect 404 not_found. (The old unversioned /api/... endpoints are gone too.)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/nope
